{
  "ticket": "Okay, so I’ve been using Northbeam for our project timelines and team assignments for the past year, and honestly, it’s been pretty solid, but lately I’ve been getting these weird emails about my account being suspended because of a failed payment, which is bizarre because I literally just updated my card last week—this was after the system told me it was processing the new one, and then all of a sudden I can’t access any of our project boards anymore, and I’m like, what’s going on? We’re in the middle of finalizing our Q2 construction schedules and if we lose access to this system, we’re going to be scrambling to manually track everything, which is not only inefficient but could cost us clients, especially since we’ve been getting a lot of complaints from our field teams about not seeing updated deadlines. I don’t know if it’s a glitch or if Northbeam’s billing system is just broken, but I did notice that when I tried to log in again yesterday, I saw a message saying 'Your workspace has been suspended due to payment failure'—this was after I thought I already fixed it. I’ve already tried reaching out to finance to double-check, but they’re saying it’s not showing up in their system, so I’m not sure where the disconnect is. Honestly, I’ve been looking at other tools like BuildFlow and ProjectPilot lately because this has been such a headache, but I really don’t want to switch now—especially not with our project timelines already tight. Can you please just fix this so we’re not stuck in limbo?",
  "category": "billing",
  "priority": "P2",
  "rationale": "A billing payment failure that has already suspended or is about to suspend the workspace is P2, as stated in the policy."
}

